{"baseRefName":"codex/platform-input-flags","body":"The local-time resolver matched only year/month/day/hour/minute. A four-second historical gap in Manaus was incorrectly marked ordinary, while nearby ordinary times received false fold flags. Match complete seconds and milliseconds before classifying candidates, preserving actual historical offsets and the existing earlier-fold/forward-gap policies.\n\nEngine candidate `0.1.1-rc.6`, stacked on #10 (`codex/platform-input-flags`, base `224863eb`). Source `fb57af7a2cd7c30983cc8fb655183d5a11f9cf30`; immutable 23-file archive at carrier `51129a197cd3f2a2a8c966fb797ea4da1e147b3d`, SHA-256 `09c3e63432f8ba2e9df05af137c42f65ab039740a207a89418d9e6470ea3db3e`. Runtime changes are confined to timezone matching and the version. The receipt schema, numerical formulas, site/starter pins and optional read-only ownership SDK remain unchanged.\n\nValidation:\n- 579 tests / 32 files on Node 22.23.2 and Node 24.19.0; required workspace build, lint, typecheck, format, package/export/checksum/neutrality and TypeDoc checks pass.\n- Two fresh consumers validate the exact packed archive, public runtime imports and TypeScript.\n- Independent copied-source review: 278 Node cases and 37 actual Chrome cases; 140 and 15 expected flag corrections respectively, with zero tested instant/offset/numerical changes. Seven actual receipt/replay controls per runtime and separate malformed/settings controls pass.\n- The initial 14 regression tests fail 10/14 on the original source. Preserve those failures, raw harness mistakes, exact identities and limitations in `docs/platform/evidence/time-seconds/`.\n\nThe original three-sample offset policy is retained; this does not certify complete transition discovery, historical timezone facts or a broad astronomical range. Separate site date-endpoint findings are documented for their own correction. No saved receipt or old artifact is rewritten. Existing SDK #5 do-not-merge/do-not-publish hold and required human/expert/legal review remain. This draft does not publish to npm or deploy the site. Existing SDK CI only targets main PRs; stacked CI acceptance is not claimed.\n\nRollback: restore the prior candidate source/pin together; retain old artifacts and receipts. Downstream site adoption requires its own reviewed source/artifact pairing and verification.\n","headRefOid":"ac27761e6dea138842e6ef5c2c69129ead7af636","isDraft":true,"number":11,"reviewDecision":"","state":"OPEN","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"StatusContext","context":"Vercel – sdk-zodia-launch","startedAt":"2026-09-08T06:15:18Z","state":"FAILURE","targetUrl":"https://vercel.com/zodiacsofficial/sdk-zodia-launch/GGgRobAeSKzyz6NrGGEqZqifCzL6"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-08T06:15:19Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://vercel.com/github","name":"Vercel Preview Comments","startedAt":"2026-09-08T06:15:19Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":""},{"__typename":"StatusContext","context":"Vercel – sdk-zodia","startedAt":"2026-09-08T06:15:17Z","state":"SUCCESS","targetUrl":"https://vercel.com/zodiacsofficial/sdk-zodia/FgHti8UdzNYyw1wg67vtRVNoJ7c5"}],"title":"Correct historical local-time gap and fold precision in engine rc.6","url":"https://github.com/ZodiacsOfficial/sdk/pull/11"}
